      "writtenOn": "2020-01-31T06:23:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is grabbing a lock and doing pretty long and heavy stuff on it, and doing that on the connectivity thread of the system. Could you make sure this is done somewhere where it doesn\u0027t do harm ?\n\nAlso a lot of this doesn\u0027t have to be done under lock. Setting the members certainly does have to, but opening a socket, building the params, all of that presumably can be done before and assigned to the member outside of the lock.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2127,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2127,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "15b7e455b2db8345253b30a324bb7d3e2e849190",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
