      "writtenOn": "2020-02-03T22:34:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not quite. The concept of a \"Child Session\" is actually rekey-agnostic.\n\nA Child Session is an abstraction over the IPsec SA pairs, and survives rekeys, while the IPsec SAs do not. This avoids the need for a user to know \"which\" IPsec SA pair a set of rekeyed SAs replaces.\n\nSo a onClosed() callback means that the server has killed our SA (eg server shutting down)",
      "parentUuid": "4226d277_f3ddd887",
